COMMENT ON COLUMN bom.customers.region IS 'Where the customer is based: North America or Europe.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN bom.products.sku IS 'Short product code used in questions: KR-6 (robot arm), SK-9 (drone), PU-3 (pump).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN bom.products.category IS 'Aerospace, Industrial or Robotics.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN bom.products.annual_volume IS 'Units of this product built per year. Multiply a per-unit saving or cost by it for a yearly figure.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN bom.products.target_unit_cost IS 'The cost the customer wants one finished unit to come in under, in USD.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN bom.products.required_certification IS 'The quality certification a manufacturer of this product''s custom parts must hold (AS9100 or ISO 9001).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN bom.products.region_restriction IS 'When ''North America'', every part of the product must come from a facility in North America. NULL means no restriction.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN bom.bom_lines.quantity IS 'How many of this part go into ONE unit of the assembly (so a part used in several assemblies must be summed).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN bom.parts.source_type IS 'custom = made to our drawing; catalog = bought from a catalog; standard = off-the-shelf.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN bom.parts.is_critical IS 'True when engineering must review any change to the part; a critical part is never swapped automatically.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN bom.parts.tolerance_mm IS 'Tightest dimensional tolerance the part needs, in millimetres. A SMALLER number is a TIGHTER tolerance.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN bom.parts.length_mm IS 'Largest outer dimension, in millimetres.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN bom.parts.width_mm IS 'Outer dimension, in millimetres.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN bom.parts.height_mm IS 'Outer dimension, in millimetres.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN bom.parts.catalog_item_id IS 'Only set for the few parts that are bought as a catalog item; NULL for custom parts. Not a replacement link: whether a catalog item could replace a custom part is decided by matching shape, material, finish, tolerance and size, never through this column.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN bom.catalog_items.min_tolerance_mm IS 'Tightest tolerance the catalog item can hold, in millimetres (smaller = tighter). It can replace a part only if min_tolerance_mm <= the part''s tolerance_mm.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN bom.catalog_items.max_length_mm IS 'Largest length the catalog item is offered in, in millimetres.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN bom.catalog_items.max_width_mm IS 'Largest width the catalog item is offered in, in millimetres.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN bom.catalog_items.max_height_mm IS 'Largest height the catalog item is offered in, in millimetres.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN bom.catalog_items.unit_price IS 'Catalog price for one unit in USD. It carries no separate duty, so compare it with the part''s landed cost.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN bom.catalog_items.distributor_certification IS 'Certification of the distributor selling the item: AS9120 (aerospace distributors) or ISO 9001.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN bom.materials.cost_per_kg IS 'Raw material price per kilogram, in USD.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN bom.suppliers.tier IS 'Tier 1, Tier 2 or Distributor.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN bom.facilities.region IS 'North America, Europe or Asia Pacific.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN bom.facilities.utilization_pct IS 'Percent of capacity in use (40 to 97). 95 or more means the facility cannot take new work.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN bom.facilities.status IS 'Operating state of the facility (all are Active); availability is judged from utilization_pct and supply_events, not from this column.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN bom.certifications.code IS 'ISO 9001, AS9100, AS9120 or NADCAP.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN bom.certifications.applies_to IS 'Manufacturers or Distributors: which kind of facility can hold it.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN bom.facility_certifications.expires_on IS 'Last day the certificate is valid. It is valid only while expires_on >= CURRENT_DATE; an expired row means the facility does not hold the certificate.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN bom.machines.tightest_tolerance_mm IS 'Tightest tolerance the machine can hold, in millimetres (smaller = tighter).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN bom.machines.status IS 'Running or Down for maintenance.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN bom.quotes.unit_cost IS 'Supplier price for one unit before import duty, in USD.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN bom.quotes.tariff_pct IS 'Import duty on this quote as a percentage (0 to 25). Landed cost = unit_cost * (1 + tariff_pct / 100).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN bom.quotes.is_current_source IS 'True for the single quote each part is bought on today; every part has exactly one current-source quote. The other quotes are alternative sources.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN bom.quotes.valid_until IS 'Date the quote expires; all current quotes run to the same date.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN bom.approved_vendors.status IS 'approved, pending or blocked. A supplier is approved for a customer ONLY when its row for that customer says ''approved''; a missing row or any other status means not approved.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN bom.approved_vendors.customer_id IS 'The customer whose approved-vendor list this row belongs to (a supplier approved by one customer is not necessarily approved by another).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN bom.work_orders.quantity IS 'Units produced in the run.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN bom.work_orders.scrap_quantity IS 'Units scrapped in the run. Scrap rate = scrap_quantity / quantity.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN bom.work_orders.status IS 'Completed or In progress.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN bom.work_orders.actual_end IS 'Date the run actually finished; NULL while In progress.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN bom.nonconformances.severity IS 'High, Medium or Low.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN bom.nonconformances.cost IS 'Cost of the defect in USD.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN bom.nonconformances.disposition IS 'What was done with the defective parts: Rework, Scrap, Use as is or Return to supplier.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN bom.engineering_changes.status IS 'Open, In review or Approved. Open and In review are still in progress.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN bom.supply_events.event_type IS 'Fire, Typhoon, Capacity constraint, Certificate lapse or Tariff change.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN bom.supply_events.severity IS 'High, Medium or Low.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN bom.supply_events.status IS 'Active (still affecting the facility) or Resolved.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN bom.purchase_orders.promised_date IS 'Date the supplier promised delivery.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN bom.purchase_orders.received_date IS 'Date it actually arrived; NULL if not yet received. Late means received_date > promised_date.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN bom.purchase_orders.unit_cost IS 'Price paid per unit in USD, before duty. Historical: it can differ from the part''s current quote.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN bom.inventory.on_hand IS 'Units in stock at the facility.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN bom.inventory.safety_stock IS 'Minimum units to keep; below safety stock when on_hand < safety_stock.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN bom.dfm_findings.saving_pct IS 'Percent of the part''s cost this suggestion would save (5 to 22). For a dollar figure apply it to the part''s landed cost on its current-source quote times the quantity used.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN bom.dfm_findings.performance_impact IS 'None means no effect on performance (safe); ''Needs engineering validation'' means it must be checked before it can count as a no-risk saving.';
COMMENT ON TABLE bom.quotes IS 'A supplier quote for a part at a facility. `unit_cost` excludes duties; the landed cost is unit_cost * (1 + tariff_pct / 100). `is_current_source` is true for the one quote each part is bought on today. Parts with a single quote have only one possible source. DEFINITION compliant source for a product: a quote whose facility (1) is in the product''s region when region_restriction is set, (2) holds an unexpired certificate matching the product''s required_certification (AS9100 for a custom part made by a manufacturer; an AS9120 distributor for catalog or standard parts), (3) has utilization_pct below 95, (4) has no Active High-severity supply event, and (5) belongs to a supplier whose approved_vendors status for the product''s customer is ''approved''.';
COMMENT ON TABLE bom.parts IS 'A part number. `source_type` is custom (made to our drawing), catalog (bought from a catalog) or standard (off-the-shelf). `is_critical` parts need engineering review before they are changed. `shape`, `material_id`, `finish`, `tolerance_mm` and the three dimensions decide whether a catalog item can replace a custom part. DEFINITION a custom part can be replaced by a catalog item when it is not critical and some catalog item has the same material, shape and finish, a min_tolerance_mm no tighter than the part''s tolerance_mm, maximum length, width and height at least the part''s, a unit_price below the part''s landed cost on its current-source quote, and a distributor certification of AS9120 when the product requires AS9100. Yearly saving = (landed cost - catalog price) * quantity used per unit * the product''s annual_volume.';
COMMENT ON TABLE bom.dfm_findings IS 'A design-for-manufacturability suggestion for a part, with the percentage it would save. It is safe when `performance_impact` is ''None''; ''Needs engineering validation'' ones are excluded from no-risk savings. DEFINITION saving per unit of a finding = quantity of the part per unit * landed cost on the part''s current-source quote * saving_pct / 100; only findings with performance_impact ''None'' count as no-risk.';
